<!--
  تاریک (Dark) palette. MIRROR of ui/theme/Color.kt (Palette.Dark) and of the CSS custom properties in
  design/preview/index.html. Three mirrors, one truth - check-theme.sh fails the build on drift.

  This file is the *default* (values/), and it is the LIGHT palette: an Android resource qualifier
  works by override, so whatever lives in values/ is also what a pre-21 device, a launcher widget,
  or a malformed night config falls back to. Light-as-default is the safe fallback (a white window
  background on a light-mode phone is correct; on a dark-mode phone the night file overrides it).

  The dark file carries the values this project shipped with, unchanged - the light theme is what was
  missing, not the dark one.
-->
